---
# Job-Seeker agent configuration — technical settings.
# (Your TARGETING criteria — markets & roles — live in data/criteria.md and are edited
#  from the dashboard. This file holds the machine settings the agents read.)
# Keys are flat "key: value" so the tiny dashboard server and the agents can both parse it.

dashboard_port: 4319

# Where approval requests are sent. Comma list of: whatsapp, chat
approval_channels: whatsapp, chat
# Your paired WhatsApp owner JID (approvals are sent here). Leave blank to auto-detect the owner.
whatsapp_owner_jid:

# Where the apply agent PAUSES for your approval before continuing.
# Comma list of checkpoints: each_section, file_upload, unknown_question, submit
apply_stop_before: unknown_question, submit

# Message tracking via your logged-in Chrome (chat-tracker, read-only, interactive/local).
# Reads your PERSONAL WhatsApp Web and LinkedIn messages — not the paired Claude WhatsApp channel.
whatsapp_web_enabled: true
# LinkedIn messages: read via Chrome by chat-tracker (read-only per ToS).
linkedin_enabled: true

# Chats that must NEVER be logged (comma list, matched as a case-insensitive prefix on the chat
# name). Group communities, family threads, anything out of scope for a job search. Empty = log
# nothing extra. The chat sweep records message CONTENT only for job-related threads anyway.
ignored_chats:

# Company aliases, so one employer known by two names does not become two records — an acquisition,
# a rebrand, an agency trading name. Comma list of `from=Canonical` pairs; the left side is matched
# case- and punctuation-insensitively. Example: acquiredco=Parent Company
company_aliases:

# Spend controls. Costs come from the run itself (claude --output-format json) and are logged to
# data/spend.md, which the dashboard reads.
# Per-run cap, passed to claude as --max-budget-usd. A run that hits it stops and says so.
max_spend_per_run_usd: 5
# Optional ceiling for the calendar month. Blank = no ceiling. When month-to-date already exceeds
# this, the scheduled run DOES NOT START and says so loudly — it is never a silent skip.
max_spend_per_month_usd:

---

# Notes

- Copy this file to `config/job-seeker.config.md` and edit. The real file is gitignored so
  your settings stay out of version control.
- `apply_stop_before` is the safety valve: the application-agent fills the form but always
  halts at these points and asks you to approve (via the channels in `approval_channels`).
- Nothing here contains personal data — that lives in `data/` and `templates/` (both gitignored).
